FindLua.cmake is vendored from CMake's own module and sets CMP0159, which only
exists in CMake 3.29 and later.  A board whose config pulls no package demanding
a newer CMake (no kodi -> no mariadb -> no host-cmake) configures with the
system cmake, and there cmake_policy(SET) on an unknown policy is a hard error:

  CMake Error at cmake/FindLua.cmake:7 (cmake_policy):
    Policy "CMP0159" is not known to this version of CMake.

Guard both policy settings.  Neither is load-bearing here: the CMAKE_MATCH_<n>
uses follow string(REGEX MATCH), not the file(STRINGS ... REGEX) that CMP0159
governs, and Lua is detected correctly either way.

--- a/cmake/FindLua.cmake
+++ b/cmake/FindLua.cmake
@@ -3,8 +3,12 @@
 # https://github.com/Kitware/CMake/blob/master/Modules/FindLua.cmake
 
 cmake_policy(PUSH)	# Policies apply to functions at definition-time
-cmake_policy(SET CMP0140 NEW)
-cmake_policy(SET CMP0159 NEW)  # file(STRINGS) with REGEX updates CMAKE_MATCH_<n>
+if (POLICY CMP0140)
+	cmake_policy(SET CMP0140 NEW)
+endif ()
+if (POLICY CMP0159)
+	cmake_policy(SET CMP0159 NEW)  # file(STRINGS) with REGEX updates CMAKE_MATCH_<n>
+endif ()
 
 unset(_lua_include_subdirs)
 unset(_lua_library_names)
